{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And the priest shall see it.</b> A decree of Scripture: the tumah of nega'im and their purification are to be only by the mouth of a priest, for שִׂפְתֵי כֹהֵן יִשְׁמְרוּ דַעַת (Malachi 2:7). They instruct the afflicted person to search his deeds and pray on his own behalf, and the priest too prays on his behalf. And besides this, by their constant examination of every nega, they acquire a trained eye for the degrees of appearances, to distinguish between one nega and another."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:11.887091995Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}